  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "Classify as faithful-stronger for the selected qualitative possibility claim. The target supplies a conservative evolution from smooth initial data to an actual discontinuity, with additional existential witness properties. Acceptance does not assert equivalence with an everywhere pointwise reading of the time derivative in equation (1.10).",
      "primary_evidence": "Attached printed pages 4–5, Section 1.1.2, assert possible spontaneous discontinuity formation from smooth initial data. The elaborated target existentially binds one flux and one evolving state satisfying conservation, initial regularity, earlier continuity, and unequal later traces."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The two substantive concerns are resolved separately: rectangle balance preserves the integral conservation framework appropriate to discontinuities, and the supplied explicit Huber definitions provide independently checkable joint satisfiability evidence. No vote or reuse hash determines these conclusions.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 explicitly supplies both integrability requirements and exact rectangle balance. The inline definitions huberSlope, huberFlux, shockState, and shockPotential provide formulas permitting the nonvacuity check below."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "The unresolved issues do not require an undetermined classification for this selected claim. Stronger analytic regularity, scalar witnesses, global temporal conservation, and an attained downward first discontinuity are properties established inside an existential conjunction, rather than assumptions restricting a universally prescribed input.",
      "primary_evidence": "The fully explicit target has no external hypotheses. D004 and D011 bind every required property to the same existential tuple. Printed pages 4–5 impose no universal quantification over fluxes or initial profiles."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "Conclusion completeness passes for the selected phenomenon. Distinct finite one-sided limits imply discontinuity of the state itself, independently of its value at the interface. D001 retains conservation across the formation event. It does not assert the displayed time derivative at every instant; that stronger interpretation is not specified by the selected discontinuous-solution passage.",
      "primary_evidence": "The final target conjuncts give left and right limits at the same positive T with qR < qL. D001 asserts mass change equals accumulated left-minus-right flux for every rectangle. Printed page 5 distinguishes failure of the classical equation from continued integral conservation."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "The exceptional-time distinction is real but does not invalidate this formalization of the possibility claim. D001 makes each interval mass locally absolutely continuous and yields equation (1.10) almost everywhere, with exact accumulated balance at every pair of times. An everywhere classical derivative requirement would be inappropriate as a general condition on discontinuous solutions: even a moving step produces an interval-mass kink when it crosses an endpoint. Other boundary cases are nonvacuous and correctly oriented.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 requires temporal integrability of each endpoint flux and exact balance for all a,b,s,t. D052 and D064 define genuine integrability and oriented integrals. D012, D037, D038, D048, and D049 use nontrivial real one-sided neighborhood filters; 0 < T and qR < qL exclude empty preformation time and zero jump."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C12 unclear",
      "resolution": "Joint satisfiability can be checked directly from the inline formulas. Choose the Huber flux, the supplied shockState, T=1, ξ=0, qL=1, and qR=-1. The initial state is -x, hence analytic. For t<1 the central branch -x/(1-t) on |x|<1-t matches the exterior branches t-x and -t-x at their boundaries, so every such spatial slice is continuous. At t=1 the exterior branches have traces 1 and -1. The Huber flux is C1 and nonaffine. Conservation follows independently from the displayed potential: its spatial derivative equals the state almost everywhere, its temporal derivative equals minus the composed flux almost everywhere, and its fixed-coordinate slices are locally absolutely continuous. Applying the fundamental theorem of calculus twice gives D001 for every real rectangle. The piecewise formulas ensure the required local integrability. Thus the conjunction is not merely formally free of empty-domain shortcuts; it has a concrete mathematical witness.",
      "primary_evidence": "Inline definitions huberSlope(u)=min(1,max(-1,u)), huberFlux as its integral, shockState, centralPotential, outerPotential, and shockPotential. The potential branches match where t=1-|x|, including (0,1). These formulas suffice for this mathematical check without using the target proof."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Existence and regularity pass. The explicit witness above satisfies the strengthened global existence package, including analytic initial data and an attained nonzero first jump. Entropy admissibility and uniqueness are not conclusions of the selected passage and are not silently inferred from the target. The target remains an existence statement within an integral conservation framework.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 5 defers detailed shock-wave theory to Chapter 11 without stating an entropy or uniqueness condition. The target and D001 contain no such predicate. The inline Huber formulas establish satisfiability of the properties actually required."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The implication holds for the selected source assertion in its discontinuous integral-conservation context. The same state begins smoothly, is spatially continuous throughout a nonempty preceding interval, and develops an actual jump at positive time while satisfying exact accumulated conservation. This does not require identifying rectangle balance with an everywhere differentiable interval-mass law.",
      "primary_evidence": "Section 1.1.2 on attached printed pages 4–5 supplies the qualitative possibility assertion and its integral-conservation context. The elaborated target and D001 provide all corresponding witness properties."
    },
    {
      "item": "Disputed regularity interpretation and dependency reuse",
      "resolution": "The blind translation correctly distinguishes outer top in WithTop ENat from ordinary infinite differentiability. D006 requires analytic Taylor coefficient functions at the outer top, so the initial regularity is stronger than smoothness. Reused arithmetic, logical, and topology declarations retain their ordinary real meanings in this target; their hashes supply provenance only. Nonaffinity is global, while the explicit nonvacuity witness also traverses the nonlinear portion of the flux, avoiding a merely unused nonlinear extension.",
      "primary_evidence": "D006, D009, D039, D041, and D043 expose the two index layers and analytic branch. D025–D035 supply the real instances. The explicit initial profile -x ranges over all real states, including the quadratic core of the Huber flux."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under the selected passage's integral interpretation of discontinuous conservation-law evolution, the existential tuple witnesses spontaneous discontinuity formation from smooth initial data. Analytic initial regularity implies smoothness; T is positive; every preceding nonnegative-time spatial slice is continuous; unequal finite one-sided traces force an actual jump at T; and D001 preserves exact accumulated conservation across that time. The scalar C1 nonaffine flux belongs to the source's nonlinear conservation-law setting. This implication does not claim an everywhere pointwise time derivative for equation (1.10)."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "The selected qualitative assertion does not entail the target's joint additional requirements: analytic initial data, a globally C1 scalar flux, conservation for all real times, continuity at every earlier nonnegative time, and a nonzero downward jump attained at that interval's endpoint. Establishing this strengthened witness requires additional mathematics, available here through the explicit formulas rather than through the source sentence alone."
    }
  },
  "classification": "faithful-stronger",
  "accepted": true,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The selected source does not specify exceptional-time conventions for the derivative in equation (1.10). Acceptance concerns its qualitative formation assertion with integral conservation; equivalence to an everywhere classical time-derivative formulation is neither established nor claimed.",
    "Standard meanings at the supplied external library frontier are retained. Foundational implementations and supplied source or dossier hashes were not independently recomputed."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "exceptional-time-conservation",
      "evidence": "D001 gives exact rectangle balance and locally integrable endpoint fluxes, yielding locally absolutely continuous interval mass and its derivative balance almost everywhere.",
      "impact": "The round-trip judge correctly identified a distinction from everywhere differentiability. That distinction limits the claimed equivalence of formulations but does not omit the selected spontaneous-formation phenomenon."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "genuine-existential-strength",
      "evidence": "The target requires analytic initial regularity, all-real-time rectangle conservation, and an attained downward jump after continuous slices. The inline Huber formulas jointly realize these conditions.",
      "impact": "The additional requirements are nonvacuous witness strength, not reduced applicability caused by extra antecedents."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "actual-discontinuity",
      "evidence": "Both traces concern q at the same positive time and location and satisfy qR < qL in the usual real topology.",
      "impact": "The statement establishes a discontinuity of the conserved state, rather than merely gradient growth, differentiability failure, or a changed value at one isolated spatial point."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached primary-source pages and inline declarations supports faithful-stronger. The source's selected assertion is qualitative possibility, and the target supplies a concrete, nonvacuous realization with additional witness properties. The rectangle predicate preserves accumulated conservation through discontinuities, while its distinction from everywhere classical temporal differentiation must remain explicit. The inline Huber definitions resolve the stronger existence concern without consulting the target proof or relying on majority agreement."
